<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Jamkhandi State</h1><p class="st-meta">1811 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Jamkhandi</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Patwardhan Brahmin state in the southern Maratha country, formed when the Patwardhan family divided its lands in 1811.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/patwardhan">Patwardhans</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chitpavan-brahmins">Chitpavan Brahmin</a> commanders of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peshwa">Peshwas</a>, held extensive <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jagir">jagirs</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishna">Krishna</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tungabhadra-river">Tungabhadra</a>. In 1811 these were divided among branches of the family, and Jamkhandi became a separate state under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gopalrao-patwardhan">Gopalrao Patwardhan</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Jamkhandi was a state of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southern-maratha-country">Southern Maratha Country</a>, later the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan-states-agency">Deccan States Agency</a>, with a Marathi-speaking ruling house over a largely <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannada">Kannada</a>-speaking population. Its rulers built schools and in the 20th century moved towards representative government.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After accession to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> Jamkhandi was merged into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bombay-state">Bombay State</a> in 1948, and since 1956 it has been part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a>, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bagalkot-district">Bagalkot district</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/jamkhandi-state.jpg" alt="Jamkhandi State" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Dr. Andreas Birken · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jamkhandiflag.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1811 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Jamkhandi</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Gopalrao Patwardhan</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Kannada, Marathi</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Jamkhandi</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1880&amp;focus=jamkhandi-state" aria-label="Jamkhandi State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6730 1564 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Jamkhandi State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7050 1820L7364 1601M7050 1820L7364 1602M7050 1820L7018 1386"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M7018 1386h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7050 1820h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7050 1820h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1880&amp;focus=jamkhandi-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
